>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `export_refute_psimp`

``` hol4
Refute.export_refute_psimp : string -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds a theorem to the model finder's partial equations.

`export_refute_psimp name` adds the theorem `name` to the theory's
`refute_psimp` set, which persists with the theory.  The model finder
uses each conjunct of the theorem as an equation for the constant
heading it when that constant has no `refute_simp` equations.  Each
conjunct must be `c t1 ... tn = u`, `c t1 ... tn` or `~(c t1 ... tn)`
for a constant `c`; the model finder drops any other conjunct with a
warning.

### Comments

The theorem attribute `refute_psimp` has the same effect.

